  grid: 10x10 (fixed); 1-cell bg=0 border surrounding 8x8 interior
  interior: split into 2x2 blocks of size 4x4 each
  template:
    location: upper-left block (rows 1-4, cols 1-4)
    content: fully filled with exactly 2 colors, no bg pixels
    symmetry: not LR-symmetric AND not UD-symmetric (ensures 4 distinct flips)
    color_balance: each color covers 6-10 of 16 cells [observed]
  quadrants:
    TL: identical to template (all 16 cells filled with the 2 template colors)
    TR: horizontally flipped template; 1-2 control pixels define color mapping
    BL: vertically flipped template; 1-2 control pixels define color mapping
    BR: both-axes flipped template; 1-2 control pixels define color mapping
  control_pixels:
    per_quadrant: exactly 1 pixel per mapped template symbol; 1-2 symbols mapped
    at_least_one_quadrant_maps_both: most quadrants map both symbols (10/12 observed)
    colors: all control colors are non-bg, disjoint from template colors
    cross_quadrant_reuse: same color MAY appear in different quadrants for different symbols
  output: each quadrant filled with its flipped template, recolored per control mapping; unmapped symbols become bg

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Set grid 10x10, bg=0, block_size n=4.
    2. Generate a random 4x4 template with exactly 2 colors (from non-bg palette), ensuring it is neither LR- nor UD-symmetric.
